<h3>glossary.html</h3><pre>
&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;
&lt;html lang="en"&gt;
    &lt;head&gt;
        &lt;meta charset="utf-8"/&gt;
        &lt;meta content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1" name="viewport"/&gt;
        &lt;title&gt;
            Glossary
        &lt;/title&gt;
        &lt;link href="static/css/style.css" rel="stylesheet"/&gt;
    &lt;/head&gt;
    &lt;body&gt;
        &lt;div class="webpage"&gt;
            &lt;!-- navigation --&gt;
            &lt;nav class="navbar"&gt;
                &lt;a class="logo" href="main.html"&gt;
                    &lt;img alt="Australian Silver Support" src="static/images/logo.png"/&gt;
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;a class="nav-item home-link" href="main.html"&gt;
                    Home
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;a class="nav-item learn-link" href="learn.html"&gt;
                    Learn
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;a class="nav-item glossary-link active" href="glossary.html"&gt;
                    Glossary
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;a class="nav-item game-link" href="escape-the-scam.html"&gt;
                    Escape the Scam
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;a class="nav-item about-link" href="about.html"&gt;
                    About Us
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;button aria-label="Read the main page content aloud" class="listen-button" id="listenButton" type="button"&gt;
                    ðŸ”Š Listen
                &lt;/button&gt;
            &lt;/nav&gt;
            &lt;!-- page content --&gt;
            &lt;main class="main" id="main"&gt;
                &lt;div class="glossary-label"&gt;
                    CYBER-SAFETY TERMS
                &lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;h1 class="glossary-title"&gt;
                    Cyber Safety Glossary
                &lt;/h1&gt;
                &lt;div class="glossary-intro"&gt;
                    Hover directly over a View meaning button to reveal only that termâ€™s definition. Hovering the card itself does nothing.
                &lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;aside class="glossary-help"&gt;
                    &lt;div class="info-icon"&gt;
                        i
                    &lt;/div&gt;
                    &lt;h3&gt;
                        How to use this page
                    &lt;/h3&gt;
                    &lt;p&gt;
                        Move your mouse over a View meaning button to see only that termâ€™s definition.
                        &lt;br/&gt;
                        Keep explanations short and easy to read.
                    &lt;/p&gt;
                &lt;/aside&gt;
                &lt;article class="glossary-card phishing-card"&gt;
                    &lt;h2&gt;
                        ! Â  Phishing
                    &lt;/h2&gt;

                    &lt;button class="meaning-button" type="button" tabindex="0"&gt;
                        View meaning
                    &lt;/button&gt;
                    &lt;div class="rollover"&gt;A fake email or message designed to trick you into giving away personal information. Phishing often uses urgency, threats or fake links.&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/article&gt;
                &lt;article class="glossary-card https-card"&gt;
                    &lt;h2&gt;
                        ðŸ”’ Â  HTTPS
                    &lt;/h2&gt;

                    &lt;button class="meaning-button" type="button" tabindex="0"&gt;
                        View meaning
                    &lt;/button&gt;
                    &lt;div class="rollover"&gt;A secure website connection that helps protect information you send online. HTTPS protects data travelling between your browser and the website, but it does not prove the website is genuine.&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/article&gt;
                &lt;article class="glossary-card malware-card"&gt;
                    &lt;h2&gt;
                        âš  Â  Malware
                    &lt;/h2&gt;

                    &lt;button class="meaning-button" type="button" tabindex="0"&gt;
                        View meaning
                    &lt;/button&gt;
                    &lt;div class="rollover"&gt;Harmful software that can damage a device or steal information. Avoid unexpected downloads and keep software updated.&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/article&gt;
                &lt;article class="glossary-card password-card"&gt;
                    &lt;h2&gt;
                        â˜… Â  Strong Password
                    &lt;/h2&gt;

                    &lt;button class="meaning-button" type="button" tabindex="0"&gt;
                        View meaning
                    &lt;/button&gt;
                    &lt;div class="rollover"&gt;A long, unique password that is difficult for another person to guess. Use different passwords for important accounts.&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/article&gt;
                &lt;article class="glossary-card two-factor-card"&gt;
                    &lt;h2&gt;
                        2 Â  Two-Factor Authentication
                    &lt;/h2&gt;

                    &lt;button class="meaning-button" type="button" tabindex="0"&gt;
                        View meaning
                    &lt;/button&gt;
                    &lt;div class="rollover"&gt;An extra security step that asks for a second proof of identity when signing in. A code sent to a trusted device is one common second factor.&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/article&gt;
                &lt;article class="glossary-card public-wifi-card"&gt;
                    &lt;h2&gt;
                        âŒ Â  Public Wi-Fi
                    &lt;/h2&gt;

                    &lt;button class="meaning-button" type="button" tabindex="0"&gt;
                        View meaning
                    &lt;/button&gt;
                    &lt;div class="rollover"&gt;A shared wireless network in public places that may be less secure than your home network. Avoid sensitive banking on unknown public Wi-Fi.&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/article&gt;
                &lt;div class="glossary-tip"&gt;
                    Tip: Keep definitions short, use familiar words and avoid unnecessary technical language.
                &lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;/main&gt;
            &lt;!-- footer --&gt;
            &lt;footer class="footer"&gt;
                &lt;a class="help-link" href="help.html"&gt;
                    &lt;span class="footer-icon"&gt;
                        â˜Ž
                    &lt;/span&gt;
                    Need help? call 1800 123 456
                &lt;/a&gt;
                &lt;div class="footer-line"&gt;
                &lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;span class="support-message"&gt;
                    We're here to support you
                &lt;/span&gt;
                &lt;span class="safe-message"&gt;
                    &lt;span class="footer-icon"&gt;
                        â™¥
                    &lt;/span&gt;
                    Stay safe, stay connected
                &lt;/span&gt;
            &lt;/footer&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
        &lt;script src="static/js/Tung.js"&gt;
        &lt;/script&gt;
    &lt;/body&gt;
&lt;/html&gt;

</pre>
